{
  "platform_id": "u5Ci7QHHRLA",
  "profile": {
    "video_id": "iron-snail:u5Ci7QHHRLA",
    "purpose": "A list of roughly ten expensive (and a few not-so-expensive) clothing items and brands that Michael is glad he bought, explaining what each is and why it earned a place on the list.",
    "video_type": "ranking",
    "thesis": "These are the pieces and brands in Michael's wardrobe that he considers worthwhile purchases, from heritage denim and jackets to boots, loopwheel tees and small craft brands.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "Glenn's Denim jeans are made entirely in the US by Glenn, a former Levi's master tailor, using denim from Red Lion Denim in Pennsylvania.",
      "Two cropped Filson jackets make the list: the Short Line Tin Cloth Cruiser and the 24 oz wool Mackinac Wool Work Jacket.",
      "Russell Moccasin Backcountry boots are chosen for true moccasin construction, a cushioned synthetic sole and their looks.",
      "The Knickerbocker x Fracap collaboration shoe boots are sold out; Fracap still sells similar styles and other collaborations.",
      "Loopwheel t-shirts are explained: the yarn is knit under no tension, giving a spongy, tough fabric that keeps its shape but is slow to make. Standard & Strange's Wakayama tee and the brand Wonder Looper are recommended.",
      "S.E.H Kelly is named a favorite brand for its old-world tailoring style and how it documents its products.",
      "The Noah NYC cotton crewneck sweater is compared with a near-identical J.Crew version, and the cheaper J.Crew one is suggested unless you want the very top of the line.",
      "Jim Green footwear from South Africa (Vellie, Razorback, Outback) is praised as good value; the boots run wide.",
      "The Wellen Easy Hemp Shirt from Huckberry is mostly organic cotton with about 10% hemp.",
      "Wythe is recommended as a brand, including its Pines Jacquard overshirt, indigo cotton linen shirt and Donegal corduroy pants."
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "title": "Favorite items introduction",
        "summary": "Michael introduces a list of purchases he loves and points to the shopping link in the description.",
        "first_segment": 0,
        "last_segment": 0
      },
      {
        "title": "Glenn's Denim jeans",
        "summary": "The story of Glenn's Denim, made in New York by a former Levi's master tailor using Pennsylvania-made Red Lion denim. These are Michael's straightest-fit jeans.",
        "first_segment": 0,
        "last_segment": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "Filson jackets",
        "summary": "The Filson Short Line Tin Cloth Cruiser jacket, its fit and patina, and how Michael lost it on the way home from Denmark. Also the 24 oz Filson Mackinac Wool Work Jacket and its cropped length.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Russell Moccasin Backcountry boots",
        "summary": "Three reasons he loves these boots: true moccasin construction, a cushioned synthetic sole for hiking and their looks.",
        "first_segment": 2,
        "last_segment": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Knickerbocker x Fracap shoes",
        "summary": "The sold-out Knickerbocker x Fracap shoe boots, which blend hiking and heritage style, break in fast and can be resoled. Other Fracap collaborations such as one with END Clothing are mentioned.",
        "first_segment": 3,
        "last_segment": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "Loopwheel t-shirts",
        "summary": "Explains loopwheel fabric and recommends the Standard & Strange Wakayama loopwheel tee and the brand Wonder Looper.",
        "first_segment": 4,
        "last_segment": 5
      },
      {
        "title": "S.E.H Kelly",
        "summary": "Why S.E.H Kelly is a favorite brand despite owning only one t-shirt from them: their photography, writing and old-world tailoring style.",
        "first_segment": 5,
        "last_segment": 6
      },
      {
        "title": "Noah NYC vs J.Crew sweater",
        "summary": "The Noah NYC cotton crewneck sweater compared with a near-identical, cheaper J.Crew version, both linked to the same creative director.",
        "first_segment": 6,
        "last_segment": 8
      },
      {
        "title": "Masterworks sponsor",
        "summary": "A sponsor read for the art investment platform Masterworks, introduced through New Balance 550 sneakers as investments.",
        "first_segment": 8,
        "last_segment": 9
      },
      {
        "title": "Jim Green footwear",
        "summary": "South African brand Jim Green: build quality, a wider fit, and the Vellie, Razorback and Outback models with comparisons to Clarks and Blundstone.",
        "first_segment": 9,
        "last_segment": 10
      },
      {
        "title": "Easy hemp shirt",
        "summary": "The Wellen Easy Hemp Shirt from Huckberry: about 10% hemp, structured, cool in heat and timeless.",
        "first_segment": 10,
        "last_segment": 10
      },
      {
        "title": "Wythe brand clothing",
        "summary": "Why he likes Wythe's summer-camp aesthetic and off-white colors, with favorite pieces including an overshirt, a shirt, corduroy pants and a leather tote.",
        "first_segment": 10,
        "last_segment": 11
      },
      {
        "title": "Outro",
        "summary": "Wraps up, notes the list isn't exhaustive, floats a regret-purchases video and previews the next day's t-shirt video.",
        "first_segment": 11,
        "last_segment": 12
      }
    ],
